{"dimension": 384, "max_elements": 100000, "ef_construction": 200, "m": 16, "ef_search": 50, "max_entries": null, "eviction_batch_size": 100, "eviction_count": 0, "memory_to_hnsw": {"b243103d-e10b-40d3-bf5e-f1f2c06bec97": 0, "518bd228-dbb9-46ce-9c18-486f80e5025d": 1, "6960c13d-54fc-43d8-ac28-972c9534833f": 2, "3fac12ef-17a9-4e3b-a06f-25e320363d44": 3, "e1ebc4e9-110b-4cf5-80a6-253765289587": 4, "0a07b4cf-bbac-40c2-89b5-765b7fbdd1a0": 5, "0a172b0a-0f73-469e-9ac3-046318e94107": 6, "a0ab4ef4-d9fc-4d45-8258-e9973f625549": 7, "068454fa-437b-43db-920e-629a193ca80a": 8, "d5ffe5ed-a072-4d30-9d68-231d16e6b11e": 9, "448150ad-007c-42d1-b5f2-779bab81bf60": 10, "29f0ddc1-37aa-4c40-83c6-114b18503724": 11, "4b322346-3af3-42f4-9119-e2d92260eeef": 12, "ed2c4cad-988f-4448-937f-fdc96e65e102": 13, "57b4346f-297d-4a29-8dcf-f75c8c3228ee": 14, "cde96da5-eda1-472c-8c5a-aa5bce739d11": 15, "1e60b7c6-c0eb-42de-8fc7-536723d62121": 16, "603287f2-a157-4c51-b5d8-b3c5ba4d2fc6": 17, "6bfeef57-f71f-4427-972f-b3f5a095439e": 18, "6d9cb469-f246-4f8e-bf5a-fb2f723c4302": 19, "a48ac2fe-75b4-43a8-954b-7e0db9bce2b3": 20, "78f1ee53-ec44-45ff-bcc5-19b13b9894c6": 21, "91f4dfe0-0be4-4192-9e95-7b42644db2a7": 22, "4c939cb5-e90f-4d3a-a876-ffcf66051761": 23}, "hnsw_to_memory": {"0": "b243103d-e10b-40d3-bf5e-f1f2c06bec97", "1": "518bd228-dbb9-46ce-9c18-486f80e5025d", "2": "6960c13d-54fc-43d8-ac28-972c9534833f", "3": "3fac12ef-17a9-4e3b-a06f-25e320363d44", "4": "e1ebc4e9-110b-4cf5-80a6-253765289587", "5": "0a07b4cf-bbac-40c2-89b5-765b7fbdd1a0", "6": "0a172b0a-0f73-469e-9ac3-046318e94107", "7": "a0ab4ef4-d9fc-4d45-8258-e9973f625549", "8": "068454fa-437b-43db-920e-629a193ca80a", "9": "d5ffe5ed-a072-4d30-9d68-231d16e6b11e", "10": "448150ad-007c-42d1-b5f2-779bab81bf60", "11": "29f0ddc1-37aa-4c40-83c6-114b18503724", "12": "4b322346-3af3-42f4-9119-e2d92260eeef", "13": "ed2c4cad-988f-4448-937f-fdc96e65e102", "14": "57b4346f-297d-4a29-8dcf-f75c8c3228ee", "15": "cde96da5-eda1-472c-8c5a-aa5bce739d11", "16": "1e60b7c6-c0eb-42de-8fc7-536723d62121", "17": "603287f2-a157-4c51-b5d8-b3c5ba4d2fc6", "18": "6bfeef57-f71f-4427-972f-b3f5a095439e", "19": "6d9cb469-f246-4f8e-bf5a-fb2f723c4302", "20": "a48ac2fe-75b4-43a8-954b-7e0db9bce2b3", "21": "78f1ee53-ec44-45ff-bcc5-19b13b9894c6", "22": "91f4dfe0-0be4-4192-9e95-7b42644db2a7", "23": "4c939cb5-e90f-4d3a-a876-ffcf66051761"}, "next_hnsw_id": 24, "metadata": {"b243103d-e10b-40d3-bf5e-f1f2c06bec97": {"memory_id": "b243103d-e10b-40d3-bf5e-f1f2c06bec97", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "On 2026-07-22, after the user approved the Acts 3\u20134 VPP transformation spec, a detailed implementation plan was saved at docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-22-japan-keynote-act3-act4-vpp-transformation.md. It specifies five internal keyframes (pause, graph, city, japan, vpp), data/layer/sequence components, concise non-technical on-screen copy, map interaction and RAF constraints, tests, screenshot, and build verification. It preserves Act 1\u20132 and the separate 100K homes closing slide. No implementation, commit, or push was performed.", "created_at": "2026-07-22T12:59:56.958452", "importance": 0.7, "metadata": {}}, "518bd228-dbb9-46ce-9c18-486f80e5025d": {"memory_id": "518bd228-dbb9-46ce-9c18-486f80e5025d", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "For Japan KubeCon keynote Acts 3 and 4, the user chose contextual, transient mini visual cues instead of a persistent story rail.", "created_at": "2026-07-22T12:28:34.348565", "importance": 0.8, "metadata": {}}, "6960c13d-54fc-43d8-ac28-972c9534833f": {"memory_id": "6960c13d-54fc-43d8-ac28-972c9534833f", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "The user wants the Act 3/4 visual storyboard retained as a reusable project artifact and may reuse its small visual cues as sidebar elements in the slides.", "created_at": "2026-07-22T12:25:44.730569", "importance": 0.8, "metadata": {}}, "3fac12ef-17a9-4e3b-a06f-25e320363d44": {"memory_id": "3fac12ef-17a9-4e3b-a06f-25e320363d44", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "The user especially likes the line 'A graph is a city, under load' for the Japan keynote Act 3/4 sequence.", "created_at": "2026-07-22T12:25:44.561271", "importance": 0.8, "metadata": {}}, "e1ebc4e9-110b-4cf5-80a6-253765289587": {"memory_id": "e1ebc4e9-110b-4cf5-80a6-253765289587", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "Act 2's Japan keynote map should be full-bleed with the JEPX chart and demand card as floating overlays; direct map interaction remains enabled while Spectacle owns arrow navigation.", "created_at": "2026-07-22T08:42:17.882502", "importance": 0.8, "metadata": {}}, "0a07b4cf-bbac-40c2-89b5-765b7fbdd1a0": {"memory_id": "0a07b4cf-bbac-40c2-89b5-765b7fbdd1a0", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "On 2026-07-22, the user approved replacing the Act 2 cold-snap MaskExtension visual with a hybrid energy-cascade network: dense, local 3D TripsLayer routes at city zoom and elevated regional transmission TripsLayer arcs as the camera zooms out.", "created_at": "2026-07-22T08:42:17.696571", "importance": 0.86, "metadata": {}}, "0a172b0a-0f73-469e-9ac3-046318e94107": {"memory_id": "0a172b0a-0f73-469e-9ac3-046318e94107", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "2026-07-22: User approved Act 2 keynote direction: a single map-led composite scene that starts with the historical 2021 JEPX price spike (10\u2192251 JPY/kWh, 25x in 40 days) and bridges to a present-day cold-snap demand scenario. It should use a 3D interactive MapLibre + Deck.gl Japan grid with geolocated homes, a MaskExtension-style demand mask, sequential camera keyframes, pointer/wheel exploration, and arrow keys reserved for Spectacle. Keep the JEPX chart as a persistent right-side sidecar, based on Texas Numbers composition. Concept asset saved at docs/planning/act2-jepx-cold-snap-map-concept.svg.", "created_at": "2026-07-21T22:42:29.353477", "importance": 0.83, "metadata": {}}, "a0ab4ef4-d9fc-4d45-8258-e9973f625549": {"memory_id": "a0ab4ef4-d9fc-4d45-8258-e9973f625549", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "On 2026-07-22, the Japan keynote Hormuz opening was enhanced with a pitched MapLibre camera, Deck.gl LNG TripsLayer, ScreenGridLayer sea-lane density, MaskExtension closure zone, and Japan grid flow TripsLayer.", "created_at": "2026-07-21T22:15:12.310117", "importance": 0.8, "metadata": {}}, "068454fa-437b-43db-920e-629a193ca80a": {"memory_id": "068454fa-437b-43db-920e-629a193ca80a", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "Japan grid utility points use animated pulse rings and star glyphs; LNG terminals use geospatial LNG text markers.", "created_at": "2026-07-21T21:09:06.130950", "importance": 0.8, "metadata": {}}, "d5ffe5ed-a072-4d30-9d68-231d16e6b11e": {"memory_id": "d5ffe5ed-a072-4d30-9d68-231d16e6b11e", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "The Hormuz map uses three visible context cards for 97% LNG transit, \u00a515,000 household impact, and 84.7% imported energy.", "created_at": "2026-07-21T21:09:05.967771", "importance": 0.8, "metadata": {}}, "448150ad-007c-42d1-b5f2-779bab81bf60": {"memory_id": "448150ad-007c-42d1-b5f2-779bab81bf60", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "On 2026-07-21 the Japan keynote Hormuz scene was retimed to 2.8s Japan\u2192Hormuz, a 1.8s hold, and a 5.2s return route.", "created_at": "2026-07-21T21:09:05.794682", "importance": 0.8, "metadata": {}}, "29f0ddc1-37aa-4c40-83c6-114b18503724": {"memory_id": "29f0ddc1-37aa-4c40-83c6-114b18503724", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "On 2026-07-21 user approved replacing screen-coordinate SVG map overlays in the keynote Hormuz sequence with geospatial Deck.gl layers over the existing MapLibre basemap, rather than embedding Kepler.gl. Rationale: Deck.gl retains precise, deterministic presenter-driven camera choreography inside Spectacle without Kepler.gl's exploratory application shell. All utility, frequency seam, terminal, Hormuz, import-flow, route, pulse, and label marks must be longitude/latitude anchored.", "created_at": "2026-07-21T20:25:02.121247", "importance": 0.7, "metadata": {}}, "4b322346-3af3-42f4-9119-e2d92260eeef": {"memory_id": "4b322346-3af3-42f4-9119-e2d92260eeef", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "Japan keynote rendering fix (2026-07-21): presentation-japan Keynote.jsx must not wrap components that use Spectacle useSteps in LazyContent, because it deregisters their step state and yields blank slides. StepBridge normalizes Spectacle's 1-based step to zero-based: Math.max(0, (rawStep ?? 1) - 1). Regression test is presentation-japan/tests/keynote-rendering.cjs and requires the Vite dev server on localhost:3100.", "created_at": "2026-07-21T19:43:22.264516", "importance": 0.7, "metadata": {}}, "ed2c4cad-988f-4448-937f-fdc96e65e102": {"memory_id": "ed2c4cad-988f-4448-937f-fdc96e65e102", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": [], "content": "## Components Built (2026-07-14)\n\n### Animation Utilities Layer\n- **useAnimeJs.js** \u2014 Timeline management hook, pause/play/reset/seek controls, cleanup on unmount\n- **animationPatterns.js** \u2014 15+ reusable animation functions:\n  - `drawPath()` \u2014 SVG stroke-dasharray animations\n  - `pulseEffect()` \u2014 Emphasis pulse\n  - `radialBurst()` \u2014 Circular expand from center\n  - `countUpNumber()` \u2014 Number count-up with formatting\n  - `colorWave()` \u2014 Cascading color change\n  - `gearRotation()` \u2014 Spinning with optional scale\n  - `svgZoom()` \u2014 ViewBox smooth transition\n  - `morphShape()` \u2014 Path morphing\n  - `flipInStagger()` \u2014 Cards flip-in effect\n  - `floating()` \u2014 Bobbing animation loop\n  - `followPath()` \u2014 Element follows SVG path\n  - `gridPattern()` \u2014 Grid/matrix reveal (spiral, wave, diagonal, random patterns)\n\n### Major Components\n\n#### 1. EnergyUsageScalingAnimation\n**Location:** `presentation-japan/src/components/EnergyUsageScalingAnimation.jsx`\n\n3-phase scaling animation: 1 home \u2192 9-building cluster \u2192 25-building city grid\n- Phase 1 (0-3s): Single home with energy pulse\n- Phase 2 (3-7s): Transform to building cluster, larger wave\n- Phase 3 (7-12s): City-scale grid with massive wave\n- Includes decorative grid background\n- Built-in info overlay showing current scale\n\n**Reusability:** Drop-in component, `autoPlay` prop controls playback, can be stepped via props\n\n#### 2. JapanGridMapAnimated\n**Location:** `presentation-japan/src/components/JapanGridMapAnimated.jsx`\n\nStep-based map animation (8 steps) showing Japan grid structure:\n- Step 0: Japan island outline\n- Step 1-2: 50Hz utilities (east) + 60Hz utilities (west) with region network paths\n- Step 3: Frequency dividing line with labels (1.2 GW capacity bottleneck)\n- Step 4: LNG terminals + import flow + pulsing indicators\n- Step 5: Hormuz strait indicator + route animation\n- Step 6: Stat boxes with count-up (15.3%, 70%)\n- Step 7: 50/60Hz seam sidebar annotation\n\n**Reusability:** `step` prop drives animation sequence, can be integrated with StepBridge\n\n#### 3. DataCenterMapOverlay\n**Location:** `presentation-japan/src/components/DataCenterMapOverlay.jsx`\n\nMap + demand forecast dual-view component:\n- LEFT: Map showing 5 planned data centers (Tokyo, Kanto, Kansai, Kyushu, Tohoku)\n- RIGHT: Mini demand forecast chart (2024: 19 TWh \u2192 2028: 35 TWh \u2192 2034: 57 TWh)\n- Status indicators: delayed (red) vs planning (amber)\n- Optional stress zone visualization showing grid impact radius\n- Stress lines connecting data centers to utilities\n\n**Reusability:** `showStress` prop toggles stress visualization, can auto-play or be stepped\n\n#### 4. AnimatedStatBox\n**Location:** `presentation-japan/src/components/AnimatedStatBox.jsx`\n\nReusable stat box component with:\n- Entrance animation (fade + slide)\n- Count-up number animation\n- Optional pulse effect on complete\n- Configurable color, delay, direction\n- Format options (percentage, integer, decimal)\n\n**Reusability:** Used throughout keynote for any stat display\n\n#### 5. ExplanationBox\n**Location:** `presentation-japan/src/components/ExplanationBox.jsx`\n\nReusable explanation component with:\n- Title + icon + stat + description layout\n- Directional entrance (up/down/left/right)\n- Underline animation on title\n- 4 presets: SELF_SUFFICIENCY, FOSSIL_FUEL, GRID_ISOLATION, LNG_IMPORT\n\n**Reusability:** Used for \"what does 15.3% mean?\" style callouts\n\n### Stagger Patterns (DRY)\nAll components use STAGGER_PATTERNS from hook:\n- LINEAR: `i * 50`\n- EXPONENTIAL: `Math.pow(i, 1.5) * 30`\n- WAVE: `Math.sin(i * 0.5) * 100 + i * 20`\n- FIBONACCI: Uses sequence\n- RANDOM: `Math.random() * 300`\n\n### Color System (DRY)\nAll animations use CSS vars + preset colors:\n- Cyan: #22d3ee (50Hz, tech)\n- Green: #10b981 (60Hz, west, healthy)\n- Amber: #FFC217 (data centers, warning)\n- Orange: #FFA35F (Hormuz, escalation)\n- Red: #ef4444 (crisis, delayed)\n- Blue: #3939D8 (grid, infrastructure)\n\n## Still Needed for Keynote\n\n1. **JEPX Pattern Slide** \u2014 Enhanced 2021 spike visualization with scaling animation (home \u2192 building \u2192 city affected by spike)\n2. **Integration with Keynote.jsx** \u2014 Wire up new components to slides\n3. **Update slide structure** \u2014 Restructure from current 22 slides to ~24-26 with expanded opening\n4. **Context compression hook** \u2014 Add to AGENTS.md\n\n## Design Principles Applied\n\n- **DRY:** Stagger patterns, colors, animation utilities centralized\n- **Composable:** Mix-and-match animations via `animationPatterns.js`\n- **Flexible:** All components accept options (autoPlay, step, color, delay, direction)\n- **Timeline-based:** All use anime.js timeline for sync control\n- **Performance:** LazyContent pattern from existing codebase ensures renders only on active slides\n- **Consistent:** All use same font families, spacing, color system", "created_at": "2026-07-14T14:16:37.752459", "importance": 0.6, "metadata": {"source_agent": "claude", "source_file": "animation_components_created.md", "content_hash": "299a4fe3db05a6c4", "synced_at": "2026-07-14T14:16:37.752186+00:00", "sync_direction": "import", "name": "animation-components-built", "description": "Keynote animation components for Japan presentation - reusable, DRY animation utilities and components", "headroom_id": ""}}, "57b4346f-297d-4a29-8dcf-f75c8c3228ee": {"memory_id": "57b4346f-297d-4a29-8dcf-f75c8c3228ee", "user_id": "lerenzomalcom", "session_id": null, "agent_id": null, "valid_until": null, "entity_refs": ["Keynote.jsx", "presentation-japan", "anime.js", "Japan", "claude.md", "agents.md"], "content": "Reference screenshot: ~/Desktop/Screenshot 2026-07-14 at 01.11.01", "created_at": "2026-07-13T23:17:09.677331", "importance": 0.95, "metadata": {"source_agent": "claude", "source_provider": "anthropic", "created_via": "tool_call", "created_at_utc": "2026-07-13T23:17:08.139318+00:00", "workspace_display": "unresolved (no memory)", "workspace_key": "", "storage_mode": "project", "_pre_ex